\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Keeping the transport of a chain}
\date{2026-11-11}

\p{Two successive links carry transports #{U_1} and #{U_2}.
An observer retaining only the endpoints records #{U_2U_1},
with the order fixed by \ref{fdip-006F}. Changing the frame
at their shared vertex inserts inverse factors between
these matrices. If a second retained transport uses the
same links, the two recorded values also share their
random input. How can the retained variables and their
joint law be specified without losing either the endpoint
frames or this dependence?}
